{# The citation protocol, shared by every profile that binds `cite_documents`.

   `citation_artefact` is the word for what the model is writing — an answer for the two
   user-facing profiles, a report for a worker — and `citation_resolver` says who turns a
   handle back into a document. A worker's handles are the lead's handles, because it runs
   on the lead's chat session; that is why its wording points at the lead rather than at
   the reader.
#}
{% if has('cite_documents') %}
When you have the answer, call {{ tool('cite_documents') }} once with the {% if web_enabled %}internal {% endif %}documents you
actually relied on, each with a quote copied exactly from the document and one line saying
what it supports. Write the handles it gives you — `[D1]`, `[D2]` — into your {{ citation_artefact }}
at the point each claim is made. Cite what you used, not everything a search returned.
{% if web_enabled %}
Web sources keep their URLs; the handles are for the user's own documents.
{% endif %}
{% if citation_resolver == "lead" %}
The lead researcher resolves them, so a handle you never allocated is no use to anyone.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
